  "name": "Harmony's Hardcore Rules",
  "slug": "harmonys-hardcore-rules",
  "teaser": "Flea market got shut down and traders no longer treat you nice - what do you do?",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/addons/0cslVch0d2vLS2yEzBGkqDhEM9h0lMHI0jEIjsGQ.png",
  "downloads": 309,
  "description": "<p>This my personal preset for SVM I use, so, feel free to use it too!</p>\n<h3>Key changes:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>No surgical meds in secure containers - they are only allowed inside special slots.</li>\n<li>No ammo in secure containers.</li>\n<li>No flea (actually, unlocks at level 55).</li>\n<li>Increased prices for almost <em>everything</em> - reduced free healing from Therapist, x1.8 multiplier for all trader prices, less items at Fence (more at crown), BTR, Taxi, etc.</li>\n<li>Less chance for insurance to return, along with the weapon/armor mods.</li>\n<li><em>And other stuff that’d make your progression harder, but not too annoying</em></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Drag and drop the zip contents in your root game directory.</li>\n<li>Open Greed.exe and down below load the custom preset (Make sure to click “Load Preset”).</li>\n<li>Click “Apply” at the bottom left corner of Greed app.</li>\n<li>Profit!</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<h2>Warning</h2>\n<p>If you had any crucial changes made on your profile before SVM, I highly suggest to <strong>NOT</strong> use this Preset for your own sake of not breaking the profile. This preset sets backpack restrictions lower, and defaults all the stash spaces. <strong>UNEXPECTED THINGS CAN HAPPEN, WHICH MAY BREAK YOUR PROFILE IF HAD SVM CHANGES BEFORE!</strong></p>\n",
